{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgvagNnefK2ZF6UuFns8j","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The contract is saved at `contract/claim.compact` and compiles cleanly with compiler 0.36.0. I only compiled it. I didn't run it or generate zero-knowledge proving keys.\n\n- **`secretKey()`** is the only witness.\n- **`publicKey(sk)`** is an exported pure circuit. It returns `persistentHash([pad(32, \"claim:pk:\"), sk])`.\n- **`claim()`** computes a nullifier from the secret key. It asserts the nullifier isn't already in the ledger set `nullifiers`, then inserts it and increments `claims`. A second claim with the same key fails with \"Already claimed\".\n- **Privacy:** the nullifier uses a different domain separator (`\"claim:nf:\"`) from the public key. The ledger holds only that hash. It never holds the secret key or the public key, so nobody can check a public key against the ledger to see whether it claimed. Using `publicKey(sk)` itself as the nullifier would have broken this."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":800,"cache_read_input_tokens":21413,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":800},"output_tokens":328,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"300cf402-0335-4148-b901-28dec6202d3c","uuid":"54bfaa52-3507-4fb9-a451-51e539a1f4f8","timestamp":"2026-11-11T05:23:04.248Z","request_id":"req_011CgvagNakTsujHfMu1xD4e"}
